        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
            <p>This proposal presents <strong>Project <span class="keyword">Atlantis</span></strong>, a groundbreaking research initiative designed to revolutionize quality of life for people with disabilities through the development of "Accessible Living Technology and Integrated Neighborhood Systems" (ATLANTIS). Drawing on the mythical <span class="keyword">Atlantis</span> as a metaphor for an ideally designed, universally accessible society, this project will create, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive ecosystem of smart home technologies, community infrastructure, and peer support networks.</p>

            <p>Led by Dr. Margaret <span class="keyword">Constable</span>, a pioneer in rehabilitation medicine and disability rights advocacy, our team will establish three living laboratories in diverse urban and rural settings to test interventions that address the social, environmental, and technological determinants of disability.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2>Research Objectives</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Develop the <span class="keyword">Constable</span> Assessment Framework for measuring multidimensional quality of life across physical, psychological, social, and environmental domains</li>
                <li>Create adaptive AI-driven assistive technologies that anticipate user needs through machine learning</li>
                <li>Design modular, affordable smart home systems for low-income disability communities</li>
                <li>Establish the <span class="keyword">Atlantis</span> Community Model: replicable templates for fully accessible neighborhoods</li>
                <li>Evaluate the impact of integrated care coordination on healthcare utilization and independence</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

