  "overview": "This longitudinal investigation examines whether chronic exposure to high-velocity sensory environments during critical neurodevelopmental windows (ages 5–8) correlates with increased incidence of Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) symptomatology. By tracking neurocognitive development across varying environmental pacing conditions—characterized by rapid visual media consumption, accelerated urban stimuli, and high-frequency information exchange—this study seeks to disentangle genetic predispositions from potential environmental triggers in attention regulation pathways.",
